  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.1",
  "name": "FlowBench",
  "description": "Overview\nSimulating fluid flow around arbitrary shapes is key to solving various engineering problems. However, simulating flow physics across complex geometries remains numerically challenging and computationally resource-intensive, particularly when using conventional PDE solvers. Machine learning methods offer attractive opportunities to create fast and adaptable PDE solvers. However, benchmark datasets to measure the performance of such methods are scarce, especially for flow physics\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/BGLab/FlowBench.",
  "alternateName": [
    "BGLab/FlowBench"
  ],
  "creator": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Baskar Group",
    "url": "https://huggingface.co/BGLab"
  },
